// Iron Deity - a battle loop on the industrial ensemble, after Nocturne.
//
// The Nocturne battle is a machine that happens to have a tune on it: an
// eighth-note bass that never stops, a kit that is more foundry than band,
// and a melody that circles a half step. This is that, at demo length.
//
// Harmony. E phrygian over a pedal, the flat second (F) as the only chord
// that is not E until the turnaround: E E F E | E E C B. The B major at the
// end is borrowed from harmonic minor so the loop leans back into its own
// top - the same dominant pull Low End is built on.
//
// The bass is one cell: root, root, octave, root, then a half-step neighbour
// on beat 3 and a walk toward the next bar. Tide's ring-modulated buzz makes
// eighths into an engine rather than a line.
//
// The kit is written as limbs. The kick is a broken three-three-two against
// the bass's straight eighths; the snare is a backbeat with a crushed
// flam on the and of four; the hats are eighths, soft on the offbeats; metal
// and anvil mark the phrase. The reverse cymbal in the intro is two seconds
// long, which at 150 is five beats: it starts on the last beat of bar 3 and
// lands on the loop's first downbeat.
//
// The toll is the bell of the Cathedral of Shadows, struck on the phrase
// downbeats. In b the lead enters over it; the chant replaces the saw
// drone, so the second half sounds bigger without a single extra note in
// the band.

title: Iron Deity
ensemble: industrial
parts: lead keys bass pad cluster:pad@pad chant:choir@pad perc metal:perc@perc
tempo: 150
meter: 4/4
key: e minor
order: intro [a b] end

section intro bars:4
  pad.drone dyn:p..mf
    | e2:16^ |
  cluster dyn:pp..mp
    | r:8 | e1:8^ |
  keys dyn:mf
    | [e3 e4]:4! | r:4 | r:4 | r:4 |
  perc.fx dyn:mf
    | boom:4! | r:4 | r:3 reverse:1 | r:4 |
  metal dyn:mp
    | r:4 | anvil:1! r:3 | r:2 clank:1 clank:1 | metal:1 r:1 metal:1 metal:1 |

